version: "2.0"
name: gnomon-adapters
description: >-
  Backend adapters: the interface a session backend implements
  (backend-adapter.ts) and its implementations, Claude Code (claude-code/) and
  local models (local/).
context:
  - >-
    Split out of packages/gnomon/.purpose (2026-10-27); path: values stay
    relative to packages/gnomon, the package root.
components:
  backend-adapter:
    description: >-
      #backend-adapter (spec §2.2 Backend drivers; declared by the 2026-10-27
      founder decision, built by T-2026-10-27-004) — the shared WIRE CODEC
      every backend driver implements, in
      src/adapters/backend-adapter.ts (types only, importing neither
      adapter): BackendAdapter<B, A, E, T> = backend id, argv(input),
      parse(line) → Tolerant<E> (the event union must have `unknown` and
      `malformed` kinds), newMeter() → UsageMeter<E>{charge(ev)}, turnLine(
      TurnInput{text, inFlight}) and interruptLine() (the backend's own
      control message, never a signal). A backend's extra channels are
      CAPABILITY interfaces — PermissionChannel (allowLine / denyLine),
      ControlChannel (errorLine / setModelLine), SdkMcpChannel
      (mcpResponseLine), SteerChannel (steerLine), ToolBrokerChannel
      (toolsSetLine / toolResponseLine / toolProgressLine; OfferedTool,
      ToolResponse) — and a concrete adapter type is the core intersected
      with only the capabilities it really has: ClaudeCodeAdapter = core +
      Permission + Control + SdkMcp (claudeCodeAdapter in
      src/adapters/claude-code/adapter.ts, #claude-adapter), LocalAdapter =
      core + Steer + ToolBroker (localAdapter in src/adapters/local/runner.ts,
      #local-runner's driver half). No optional members and no fake methods:
      claudeCodeAdapter.steerLine is a compile error. There is no
      normalized cross-backend event vocabulary; each adapter keeps its own
      event union. src/adapters/index.ts holds BACKEND_ADAPTERS (by id) and
      AnyBackendAdapter; src/adapters/line-splitter.ts the §3.3 capped line
      splitter both lanes use. The lanes carry out start / send / stop with
      it, each binding `const drv` (src/kernel/supervisor/supervisor.ts for
      claude-code, src/kernel/supervisor/local-session.ts for local); the
      process halves (spawn, sandbox, permits, trace, broker) stay in each
      lane; session.open{backend: claude-code | local} picks one (supervisor
      port.ts). Conformance: test/backend-adapter.test.ts replays every
      adapter over each of its fixtures (src/adapters/<backend>/fixtures/
      <version>-turn.jsonl + .expect.json, schema
      gnomon-adapter-replay:v1: kinds, types, charged; G-ADP-01 claude-code,
      G-ADP-02 local), fuzzes parse (never throws), checks the tolerant
      kinds, and poisons every model-text string (text, content, delta,
      result, thinking) to show usage is never read from model text.
      session-supervisor.test.ts also replays the synthetic claude fixture
      through a live session (fake claude's mode.replay): each driver line is
      a turn.event in order, seq contiguous, the session still running.
      The nightly RECORDED re-record per backend version is a todo (needs a
      trace extractor and scheduled CI; local needs a lane tee); both
      fixtures today are synthetic (their expect.json says source).
    path: src/adapters/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, adapter, backend, paradigm-8]
    related: ["#claude-adapter", "#local-runner", "#supervisor"]
    tests:
      - test/backend-adapter.test.ts
      - test/claude-adapter.test.ts
      - test/local-runner.test.ts
      - test/session-supervisor.test.ts
    oracles: [G-ADP-01, G-ADP-02]
  claude-adapter:
    model-guard: >-
      Model picker (Aegis): buildClaudeArgv refuses a model that fails
      contracts claudeModelProblem with a TypeError, because `--model` takes
      the NEXT argv token whatever it is (a value like --verbose or
      --dangerously-skip-permissions would be eaten as the model or reach
      claude's parser). Defence in depth behind the supervisor's own check.
    usage-split: >-
      #ledger-mod (K2 feed v2): parseStreamLine's result event also carries
      split {in, out, cacheRead, cacheWrite} = usageSplit(result.usage)
      (numbers only; Aegis L2: each floored and clamped to a safe integer at
      the source, so the logged row equals the feed projection); the total and the
      UsageMeter charging are unchanged.
    backend-scope: >-
      TD-2026-10-19-252 (spec §1, §2.2, §22 item 26): backends are Claude
      and local models only. Other agents (opencode, grok, ...) get their
      own driver later, each with its own law-7 billing ruling; there is no
      generic ACP passthrough.
    description: >-
      #claude-adapter (spec §2.2, §3.3; M1.7 slice 1) in
      src/adapters/claude-code/adapter.ts. P8-D96: argv --permission-prompts
      host --permission-prompt-tool stdio (assertPermissionChannel throws on
      any other value); events permission-request / control-cancel /
      control-request-unknown; stdin permissionAllowLine /
      permissionDenyLine / controlErrorLine (never updatedPermissions). SLICE 2 (T-2026-10-18-010 L4):
      SESSION_HOOKS_MODES all|user-only|none and settingSourcesFor(mode) ->
      --setting-sources; the mode is the root-signed config.sessions.hooks
      (budget/config.ts parseSessionsSection; default all; rollback/invalid
      after a signed config => none), wired by the daemon into #supervisor
      and logged as session.sandbox.settingSources. P8-D97: pluginDirs
      (--plugin-dir) and addDirs (--add-dir), deduped; repoContextFor(mode)
      is true for audited only. Q6: EXTRA_FLAGS allow-list (--max-turns,
      --no-session-persistence) and ARGV_GRAMMAR/assertArgv (each kernel flag
      once; --agents/--tools never; one variadic --add-dir). The §3.3 argv with FORBIDDEN_FLAGS
      throwing (G-RUN-01, also --flag=value and extras); stream-json parse,
      TOLERANT (unknown fields ignored, unknown types `unknown`, non-objects
      `malformed` — the falsifier); UsageMeter charges each message id once
      and the result only its remainder; 4 MiB line cap; the stdin user and
      control_request interrupt lines. fixtures/2.1.302-turn.jsonl replays
      the shapes p10m-claude-compat-generated observed (G-ADP-01, synthetic;
      recorded nightly replay is slice 2). Founder 2026-10-23:
      --include-hook-events (kernel-owned, exactly once, never an extra):
      system.hook_started{hook_id, hook_name, hook_event} and
      system.hook_response{…, output, stdout, stderr, exit_code, outcome}
      (claude 2.1.309; no command, no duration) parse as `unknown` and are
      turn.event rows like every line (the sensitive kind's redaction, big
      lines by hash); #gui-turn-steps reads them, the kernel acts only on a
      blocking Stop response (#offer-router). Aegis 2026-10-23: M2
      hookFactsOf reads {id, event, name, exit, outcome, blocked} from the
      FULL line and #supervisor logs it as turn.event.hook (kernel-set, also
      when the line goes by hash); stopHookBlocked lives here. L2
      hookStoredLine: a hook_response's stdout / stderr / output stay inline
      only up to HOOK_OUTPUT_INLINE_CAP (4 KB) each, redacted by trace's
      redactText, else {bytes, sha256}; output = stdout + stderr is dropped;
      the row adds lineHash, bytes and lineKept{hashed, dropped, redacted}.
      L3 (#kernel-log redaction.ts): SESSION_NEVER_FIELDS hides a
      hook_response row's line and lineHash from a session reader, even its
      own (the hook facts stay). Claude's synthetic user line (Stop hook
      feedback, isSynthetic) is hook output too: syntheticStoredLine caps
      and redacts each text block the same way, the row says
      `synthetic: true`, and the session-reader rule hides its line and
      lineHash (an older row is matched by "isSynthetic":true in the line);
      a real user line is stored as received. #backend-adapter: claudeCodeAdapter (ClaudeCodeAdapter = core + PermissionChannel + ControlChannel + SdkMcpChannel) wires these free functions, UsageMeter.charge(ev) is the meter entry the supervisor calls, and LineSplitter moved to src/adapters/line-splitter.ts (re-exported).
    path: src/adapters/claude-code/
    type: module
    tags: [gnomon, adapter, stream-json, paradigm-8, m1.7]
    implements: "#backend-adapter"
    related: ["#backend-adapter", "#local-runner"]
    tests:
      - test/claude-adapter.test.ts
    oracles: [G-RUN-01, G-ADP-01]
